# Line endings that are load-bearing rather than cosmetic.
#
# cmd.exe needs CRLF: a .cmd checked out with LF endings misreads labels and
# goto, and one that gains a BOM tries to execute the BOM as part of its first
# line. A shell script needs the opposite — a CRLF .sh fails with "bad
# interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which names nothing useful.
#
# Pinned here because the defaults only hold by luck: a clone on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites both, and nothing in the repository would notice
# until someone on Windows double-clicked a file that no longer runs.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
